id: pm-449do9
title: "2026.8.1 regression: governance dedupe audit rejects the restored all-lifecycle status sentinel"
description: "Current main at pm 2026.8.1 again rejects pm dedupe-audit --status all, although closed pm-mp49 records that exact package-owned contract as implemented and verified. Omitting --status considers all 2,263 items. This recurrence preserves the completed historical record and owns only the new drift across behavior, docs, contracts, recovery guidance, and tests."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: agent-ux,"area:contracts","area:extensions",dedupe,governance-audit,regression
created_at: "2026-08-01T20:20:19.401Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-05T18:34:28.323Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-05T18:34:27.829Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-05T18:34:27.829Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "Explicit --status all succeeds and considers the same all-lifecycle candidate set as an omitted status filter; Result metadata truthfully records the explicit all sentinel; Help, action contracts, docs, completions, SDK/package handler, focused tests, and packed installed-consumer behavior agree; Configured custom statuses remain accepted and invalid statuses still fail with the declared domain; A regression gate prevents the package-owned parser from drifting from the shared lifecycle-filter contract"
goal: project management = context management
objective: Restore one explicit all-lifecycle duplicate-scan grammar across core and package-owned surfaces
value: Agents can follow duplicate-prevention guidance without an undocumented omission workaround
impact: "Removes a live contradiction between CLI behavior, documentation, recovery text, and immutable completion evidence"
outcome: "All-status duplicate sweeps are explicit, portable, tested, and stable"
why_now: The mandatory all-status inventory reproduced the regression before new tracker work was added
parent: pm-ugqx
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: medium
environment: pm 2026.8.1 built from current main with pm-governance-audit active
repro_steps: Run pm dedupe-audit --mode title_exact --status all --limit 10000 --json; compare with the same command omitting --status.
resolution: Governance dedupe uses the shared lifecycle parser and strict complete SDK collection with per-workspace registry isolation.
expected_result: Explicit all and configured alias CSV filters agree with shared contracts; limits bound clusters after complete collection.
actual_result: Concurrent real workspace regressions pass and the installed package considers all three temporary items with a one-cluster limit.
affected_version: 2026.8.1
component: pm-governance-audit/dedupe-audit lifecycle filter contract
regression: true
customer_impact: Agents following repository guidance cannot express the required all-status duplicate scan explicitly and receive contradictory recovery guidance.
